---
description: Folder layout, barrels, type placement, and import paths
globs:
  - "**/*.ts"
  - "**/*.tsx"
---

Project conventions win. Read the surrounding tree first; these apply when adding a new area.

## Folders

❌ components/  hooks/  utils/  types/          // grouped by kind
✅ pages/orders/components/order_list/
     streams_view.tsx  utils.ts  utils.test.ts
Feature folders. Top-level `components/`, `hooks/`, `util/` only for genuinely cross-feature code.

❌ streams_view/index.tsx                       // when the folder also holds tests, hooks, utils
✅ streams_view/streams_view.tsx
`index.tsx` only when the folder holds a lone component and nothing else.

Files and folders are `snake_case`, hooks included: `use_device.ts`. One hook per file, named for it.

## Barrels

❌ components/index.ts re-exporting every sibling
✅ import { StreamsView } from './streams_view/streams_view';
No barrels in app code; import from the defining file. A barrel is a published package's public
entry point, nothing else. Delete dead re-exports when you find them.

## Types

❌ src/types.ts holding every domain model
✅ the type lives with the module that owns it; shared types move to the closest common ancestor

## Imports

✅ import { StreamsView } from './streams_view/streams_view';   // within a feature
✅ import { formatDate } from '@/utils/date';                   // across features or packages

❌ import { type IFoo, bar } from './foo';
✅ import type { IFoo } from './foo';
   import { bar } from './foo';
Inline `type` only when values and types genuinely come from one module.

Circular dependencies are banned. Break the cycle by extracting the shared piece.
Import ordering is enforced by `simple-import-sort`; do not hand-sort. See
eslint-recommendations.md for the group configuration.
